Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma left breast at 3 o clock with DCIS positive at the anterior margin after re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY SAMPLING  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND  0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm unoriented left simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a 25 7cm brown skin ellipse with an eccentric 7 5cm areola  Centrally within the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unremarkable nipple which comes to 5 5cm of the closest skin margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm curvilinear scar bordering the areola along the probable inferolateral aspect  Also noted is a second REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar also along the probable inferolateral aspect  The scars are REMOVED_DATE and 1 5cm of the closest probable inferolateral skin margin  Also noted along the probable upper outer aspect of the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink brown papule which comes to 0 3cm of the skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue and yellow orange discoloration