Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 50 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old Asian female  status post ultrasound guided core biopsy   right breast ovoid hypoechoic solid mass at 9 o clock  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm    fibroadenoma versus carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES  DIFFUSE LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  Sections show a dense diffuse infiltrate of medium sized and large atypical lymphoid cells with oval or slightly irregular nuclei  prominent nucleoli and scant cytoplasm  Mitoses are frequent  Occasional tingible body macrophages are present  The histologic features are consistent with lymphoma and immunostains support the diagnosis   See addendum   Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 07                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains  kappa  lambda  there is monotypic cytoplasm  Ig kappa  staining of many lymphoid cells in a diffuse pattern  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibodies to T lineage associated antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of rare small cells scattered within the tissue  With antibody to cytokeratin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 cam 5 2  there is no staining of tumor cells  The cells are also positive for bcl 2 and many are positive for bcl 6  Overall  approximately 70  of the tumor cells stain for Ki 67  proliferation   Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of diffuse large B cell lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   are multiple cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A and B  Gross Description by  JULIE ZWIRBLE Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Diane R Fingold  M D  Helenanne D alessandro  M D  John Henry Eichhorn  M D  Lan Wang  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES , 2.3.
